# Exact-Package Capture Qualification

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M4 Qualified candidate
Dependencies: 14_PACKAGING_RELEASE.todo

## Purpose

Determine which exact sharing configurations can be honestly supported for the packaged app.

## Tasks

- [ ] Freeze the required product/build/backend matrix approved in workstream 01.
- [ ] Run TODO\WORKFLOWS\02_CAPTURE_QUALIFICATION.todo against the exact package SHA-256.
- [ ] Record positive controls, API results, shell/picker observations, local visibility, and remote frames.
- [ ] Qualify Teams/Zoom desktop and Meet Chrome/Edge screen/window/tab modes actually required.
- [ ] Qualify each exposed required OBS Display/Window Capture backend independently.
- [ ] Exercise current C01-C18 scenarios, startup under active sharing, and secondary-surface exposure.
- [ ] Inspect independent recipient output and available applicable meeting recordings separately.
- [ ] Capture frame counts/gaps and review transitions; use OCR only as an aid.
- [ ] Record untested hardware, optional paths, unavailable recording access, and unsupported modes.
- [ ] Publish a sanitized candidate support table and file defects for even a single content-leak frame.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every required row passes on the exact package, or the owner explicitly changes the release scope.
- [ ] Whole-screen claims are not inferred from isolated tab/presentation-window results.
- [ ] Black/stale rectangles, picker entries, text leakage, and API errors are separately classified.
- [ ] No local preview, missing recording, negative OCR result, or assumed backend substitutes for evidence.
- [ ] Support wording states exact versions, tested environments, date, and non-universal limits.

## Completion evidence

- None. docs\QUALIFICATION.md starts all qualification candidates NOT_TESTED.
- Research and spike evidence, once created, will not by themselves satisfy this package gate.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-07 - Planned; packaging intentionally precedes final qualification.
